WEBVTT

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.480
Daddy.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.690
I had a dream.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:13.860
Joonsang and I were here as man and wife to say "hello" to you.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.280
We even sat here and drank together,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.500
and showed you that we were a good couple.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.210
And then we stayed like that for a long time...

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.420
For a very long time...

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.010
I must have liked Joonsang so much

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.520
because we were one from the start, weren't we?

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:43.730
That's why I liked him, right, Daddy?

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.730
I guess I shouldn't dream anymore.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.570
Should I, Daddy?

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.110
<i>Joonsang...</i>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.330
<i>Bye, Joonsang.</i>

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.890
Come on, throw it to Daddy.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.760
Here I go!

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.140
Okay.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.480
Look how much you've recovered!

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.480
Here you go.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.250
Looks like Daddy missed.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.150
Why don't you go over to that man and ask for the ball?

00:02:58.570 --> 00:02:59.740
Say, "Could I have the ball, Mister?"

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.670
Here it comes!

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.630
Huh?

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.170
Somebody!

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.180
Is he all right?

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.200
Is that man okay, Daddy?

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:25.680
Hello?

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.970
Are you all right?

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:29.660
Get a hold of yourself!

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:30.930
Can you hear my voice?

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:34.610
Have you still not heard back from Joonsang, Manager Kim?

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.500
His cell phone seems to be off.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.190
Even the people at his company don't know where he is.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.820
Keep calling him.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.740
You need to leave for the airport right now,

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.080
if you want to be on time for your concert.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.500
That's fine; just find Joonsang first.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.760
What's going on, Seungryong?

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.340
Why's Yujin quitting all of a sudden?

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.680
Try talking her out of it, will you?

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.060
What are you doing, Yujin?

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.690
I figured I'd pack up early, before I inevitably get fired.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.360
What are you talking about, Yujin?

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.400
I just want some time to think

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.450
about what I can do, and what I should be doing.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:26.620
I want to think it through from the beginning again.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.870
I know things aren't easy for you right now, but don't do this.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.870
Here, I'll give you some time off.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.710
Go rest, okay?

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.170
Remember this, Jeong-a?

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:38.880
The Impossible House?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.380
When something's "impossible" it means it can't be done.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.380
I wonder why I've been holding on to this idea for so long.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.890
Well, you never know.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.000
Nah.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.810
I want to give up on what's impossible now.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:56.940
I want to quit.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.570
What's going on?

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.910
I haven't been able to reach you this whole time.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:09.910
I thought you were trying to never see me again?

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.740
Come on, stop embarrassing me.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.960
I'm only saying this because the idea of it makes me sad.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.460
Should I just go back then?

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.420
Nah, thanks for coming.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.970
Sorry I made you worry.

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:31.630
Let's go to the seolleongtang restaurant behind the annex building;

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:33.220
I'm craving the kkakdugi they have there.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.850
What are you talking about?

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.270
You quit your job?

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.920
I've been kind of absent-minded lately,

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.640
so I figured I don't want to cause Jeong-a more trouble

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.240
by holding progress back like this.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:49.110
What are you going to do, now that you've quit?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.910
I haven't really thought about it.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.830
Well, get some rest.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.540
Getting rest probably isn't a bad idea.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.970
Could you let me see Joonsang?

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.260
I haven't been able to get a hold of him.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.060
Just forget about him.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:17.850
I'll help you until you do.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:22.860
You don't have to worry about me. As you can see, I'm fine.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.490
I know that we have the same father.

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:32.660
So you knew too, huh?

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:40.450
Please, I just need to see him one last time.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:41.960
Just once is all I need.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.500
Joonsang and Yujin are siblings?

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.340
They have the same father?

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.260
Does Yujin know about this?

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.010
Sanghyuk too?

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.060
He's the one who told me.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.690
I don't get it.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:05.570
Why are you telling us this, Chelin?

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:10.950
We would have been better off not knowing.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:15.080
You guys went all the way back to our high school

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.540
to throw an engagement party for Yujin and Sanghyuk, right?

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.600
I'm telling you now so you guys don't try anything like that again.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:25.200
"Don't go around doing useless things and making the situation worse,"

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:26.290
that's what I'm saying.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:32.760
Poor Yujin.

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:34.930
Poor, poor Yujin...

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.150
See this here?

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:41.520
This is a chronic subdural hematoma.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.750
We haven't been able to see this until now

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.820
because the blood has been coagulating slowly ever since the accident.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.780
I'll make arrangements for your surgery right away.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.780
Will the surgery solve the problem?

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.870
It'll at least inhibit further deterioration.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:01.910
If we let this go untreated,

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:04.750
the hematoma will cause pressure on the optical nerves and the augen,

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.420
and you'll lose your vision completely.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.840
You'll experience a deterioration of brain function after that.

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:11.840
Ultimately, it could even lead to death.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:15.300
Will I experience any side or after effects from the surgery?

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.150
Since it is neurosurgery,

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:23.850
you may or may not experience a deterioration in memory.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:27.360
Does that mean I might even lose some of my memories?

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:32.110
We cannot discount the possibility of that happening.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:33.550
There's no time to lose;

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:35.030
this must be dealt with immediately.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:09.770
Sorry if this is taking a long time because of me.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:11.980
It usually takes this long.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:15.860
But the traffic's jammed and it's raining on top of that.

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:18.740
It was the same ten years ago, remember?

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:24.620
The day of Joonsang's "funeral", the day after that,

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.160
and the day after that were all like this.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.420
You didn't cry, Yujin.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:33.340
I think it must take a lot of time for true sadness

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:35.180
to really sink in.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.390
So don't try too hard to force yourself to forget.

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:43.180
Okay.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:09:59.450
Hello?

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:02.280
Is that you, Joonsang?

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.440
Where are you?

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:05.950
Why didn't you answer your phone?

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:06.850
You had me so worried.

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:08.910
I thought you couldn't make it,

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.310
but I'm glad that I was able to see your face before I left.

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:15.610
I only stopped by to tell you something.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.030
I heard you were going to wrap up things here

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.280
and go back to the main office in the States.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:21.780
Is that what you wanted to tell me?

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:26.280
Then what?

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.290
This will be the last time.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.660
The last time?

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:34.460
You'll never see me again.

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:41.760
You told me once, when I asked about my father, that he's dead, right?

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:48.350
You'll answer the same way whenever someone asks you about me.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:13.370
Boarding will start soon; we'll have to hurry.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:49.030
It's the picture you guys took at the photo studio.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.460
How did you know I'd be here?

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.130
One of the people I work with is a fan of Ms. Mi Hee.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:00.980
I heard that she was leaving the country today,

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:02.550
so I thought you might be here too.

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:04.630
I see.

00:13:05.230 --> 00:13:08.550
I couldn't find any way to reach you after you left the hospital.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:11.640
Oh yeah, did you get your test results back yet?

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:13.520
You're fine, right?

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:16.730
They said it's nothing serious.

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:18.940
Thank goodness.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.780
There's something I need you to help me with.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:25.530
What is it?

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:27.910
I'm asking this as a favor between friends.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:30.030
Friends?

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:33.540
So we're finally friends?

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:35.750
It took a long time, didn't it?

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:37.330
It's taken ten years.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:39.990
Yeah.

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:41.500
And it turned out to be so easy.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:45.760
Why do you think it was so hard for us to take things

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:48.340
one step at a time back then?

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.220
This is about Yujin, right?

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:56.850
What can I do for you?

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:59.850
I'll do whatever you ask.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.650
It will probably be better for you to have the surgery in America,

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:17.000
as they have a more qualified team for it there.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.620
But I recommend that you leave immediately,

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.500
as the long flight there could have adverse effects 

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:22.790
on your body.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:26.390
Please don't hesitate to call me if you need assistance,

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:27.300
even when you're there.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.720
Thank you.

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:33.390
I'm also currently experiencing temporary losses of peripheral vision,

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:36.560
and at times a slight darkening of vision...

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.400
Those are symptoms that your augen and optical nerves

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.730
are under pressure from the hematoma.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:47.690
You must hurry; otherwise, you might lose your vision completely.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:52.570
So you're going Parisienne on us too, now?

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:56.830
It's bad enough that Chelin's all Parisienne already, but you too?

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:58.710
Boy am I in for a world of trouble.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:00.750
What are you talking about?

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:03.380
You better not come back and act all pompous

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:04.880
just because you went to study abroad, okay?

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.760
Don't you worry about a thing.

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:14.210
I guess I'll have to move out of this place once you're gone.

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:15.430
I like this place too.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:17.130
Nah.

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:19.230
Just live here until you get married.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.600
Married?

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:25.820
I need to find a man before I can do that.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:27.940
You've got Yongguk, haven't you?

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.320
N-No way!

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:32.130
We're not like that, okay?

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:33.950
Don't even joke about that!

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.910
Why don't you guys go to Paris for your honeymoon, while I'm still there?

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:39.950
I'll be a good guide, I promise.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.580
Stop it!

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.040
When should we throw your going-away party?

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:47.370
We should pick a day and then go nuts all night long with all our friends,

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:48.760
just like old times.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.970
Yeah, sounds great.

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:53.090
You should invite the people at work too,

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.890
since our posse is pretty much just

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:57.430
Sanghyuk, Yongguk, Chelin,

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.470
and Joonsang...

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.150
S-Sorry.

00:16:02.150 --> 00:16:04.480
Why am I such a ditz?

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:07.480
It's okay.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:10.650
Stupid, stupid, stupid!

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:20.910
It's me, Yujin.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.750
I'm in front of your house right now.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.670
Could I see you for a minute?

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.420
What are you doing?

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.640
What would going out accomplish?

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.430
What could seeing Joonsang possibly accomplish?

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.640
How do I look? Pretty?

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:46.810
Does it matter if you do?

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:48.310
Maybe not,

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:51.940
but I want him to remember me as being pretty.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.350
What's wrong with you?

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:56.610
So what if he remembers you as being pretty?

00:16:56.960 --> 00:16:57.990
Don't go.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.450
Nothing good can possibly come of seeing him, Yujin!

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.000
What's wrong with you?

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.120
It's all over, remember?

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:07.130
I'll be back.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:28.690
Hey!

00:17:35.250 --> 00:17:36.800
Why do you look so pale?

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:38.360
You look like you're sick.

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:41.000
It must be because I've been busy.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:42.990
I had to take care of stuff here and there.

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.410
So you're really leaving?

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.670
I'm leaving these sketches with you.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:54.170
The Impossible House?

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:55.930
Yeah.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:57.840
I leave it to you now.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:00.550
I only said I was going to help.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:04.680
I want you to finish it for me.

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:08.350
Are you all right?

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:10.610
What about you?

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:13.570
I love you.

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:19.160
I've always loved you, and I always will.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:24.370
I don't care what anyone says or thinks.

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:29.370
I don't feel embarrassed or ashamed by it.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:32.540
They have no idea how hard it's been for me;

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:35.250
they don't know what my heart had to go through.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:39.470
Every moment I've spent with you is precious to me.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:42.600
Yujin...

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:46.310
I'm not going to forget anything.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:50.310
I'll remember all the moments we've shared together.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.210
Don't see me off at the airport tomorrow.

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:16.840
I won't.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:19.050
And Yujin, let's...

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:24.010
never meet again.

00:19:25.520 --> 00:19:29.770
Let's just cherish the time we spent at the ocean as our last,

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:32.770
and never meet again, savoring only those good times we had.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:36.520
Could you do that for me?

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.820
Yeah, I promise.

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:43.110
Thanks.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:48.790
Joonsang, let's both promise not to look back at each other, okay?

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:53.790
I don't want our backs to be the last thing we see of each other.

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:57.210
Okay.

00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:00.010
You have to keep your promise, okay?

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:04.010
Don't look back.

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:42.800
Hello?

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:44.010
<i>We're calling from the hospital;</i>

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.090
<i>could I talk to Mr. Joonsang Kang? This is urgent.</i>

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.140
What is it?

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:51.560
<i>Mr. Kang forgot one of the documents he needs</i>

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.060
<i>for his surgery in America.</i>

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:55.300
Surgery?

00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:58.560
I thought the test results came back fine?

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:01.000
<i>He's barely holding on;</i>

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:02.740
<i>his condition is very dangerous.</i>

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:05.550
<i>Surgery is his only chance,</i>

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:07.780
<i>but I can't guarantee that it'll be successful.</i>

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:10.550
<i>Hello?</i>

00:21:10.550 --> 00:21:13.080
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.150
You eat too, Mom.

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:43.700
Maybe I should have cooked some fish as well;

00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:45.490
you won't be able to eat too much of it in France.

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:47.950
You keep eating,

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:49.570
it won't take long for me to make it.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:50.950
Mom...

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:58.050
Don't cry;

00:21:58.050 --> 00:22:00.840
it's not like I'm going to die, you know.

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:04.960
It hurts me because it feels like you're running away.

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:07.170
I'm not running away;

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.200
I'm going there to study.

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:10.970
Don't tell me you're getting second thoughts about letting me go?

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:14.350
You're really okay, right?

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:15.800
It's not too late;

00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:18.350
you can just come live here with me, if it's too hard for you.

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:22.150
I'll be fine while I'm there, Mom.

00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:25.280
Yujin.

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:30.360
Don't worry. I'll eat and sleep properly, and...

00:22:33.530 --> 00:22:35.790
I won't cry any more.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:41.880
I can't see which bowl I'm eating out of because you made me cry.

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:43.550
Sorry.

00:22:43.550 --> 00:22:44.960
Keep eating.

00:22:45.130 --> 00:22:46.260
You eat too, Mom.

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:50.200
If we do that, we'll be using the same song as the opening segment,

00:22:50.200 --> 00:22:51.510
so let's just change that bit.

00:22:52.180 --> 00:22:53.790
Why don't we use "Spring", from Vivaldi's "Four Seasons",

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:56.020
since spring's right around the corner?

00:22:56.850 --> 00:22:59.520
That's too cliché.

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:03.310
Yeah, yeah, I'm all about clichés, I get it.

00:23:04.270 --> 00:23:06.280
Just do whatever you want, Producer Kim.

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:10.320
Let's see you choose a better song for the opening segment.

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:12.250
I was just joking.

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:13.410
Wait up!

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:19.830
<i>Joonsang left, as did Yujin shortly thereafter:</i>

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:22.290
<i>to France, not New York.</i>

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:26.130
<i>And winter ended just like that.</i>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:29.970
<i>Every winter has its end,</i>

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:34.180
<i>but we had no idea back then</i>

00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:39.350
<i>that Joonsang and Yujin's winter was not over yet.</i>
